# Files this repo deliberately does NOT carry from its template.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. Every repo in this tree merges from a `stem` remote. A file
# that a descendant has deleted is not a settled decision as far as git is
# concerned: the next time the template TOUCHES that file, the cascade stops
# with a modify/delete conflict, and whoever is running it has to work out from
# scratch whether the deletion was deliberate. That has already happened
# repeatedly for `sending-indicator.e2e.ts` in bleeps and mandalas, and the only
# record of the intent was a commit message from months earlier.
#
# Listing the path here does not change what git does - the conflict still
# happens - but it makes the answer a lookup instead of an excavation, and
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` turns the resolution into one command.
# `web/test/offshoot-omissions.test.ts` fails if any listed path comes back, so
# a cascade that silently reintroduces one cannot be committed quietly.
#
# FORMAT. One path per line, relative to the repo root. `#` starts a comment.
# Give every entry a reason: the next person's question is never "which file",
# it is "why", and an unexplained list is how a deletion outlives the reason for
# it and becomes cargo cult.
#

web/e2e/tests/sending-indicator.e2e.ts
# The template's sending-indicator suite, deleted here long before this list
# existed and re-decided by hand at every cascade since. It asserts the order
# and floor of the two in-flight rungs, which this app does not present. The
# escape-hatch suite, which shares the same fixture, IS carried here.

web/e2e/tests/home.e2e.ts
# The template's home-page suite. This repo has never carried it - it has its
# own home page and does not assert on it - and the cascade offered it back
# twice in one afternoon when the template changed how it reads the app name.

